---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: 'About Buoy Money',
    url: `${SITE.url}/about`,
    publisher: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#org` },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE.url },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: `${SITE.url}/about` },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Buoy Money builds a personal-finance app around count-up budgeting, a system designed to make saving feel like winning instead of going without."
  path="/about"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">ABOUT</p>
      <h1>I think budgeting has the psychology backwards.</h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:clamp(32px,5vw,56px)">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>
        Most budgeting tools are built on subtraction. You start the month with a number
        and watch it shrink with every purchase, until the "win" is a small, anxious
        balance and the lesson is that spending equals loss. For a lot of people, that
        framing is exactly why budgeting never sticks.
      </p>
      <p>
        Buoy Money is built on the opposite idea, <a href="/count-up-budgeting">count-up
        budgeting</a>. Each spending category earns a small allowance every day, and the
        number you watch <em>grows</em> when you underspend. Saving becomes a visible,
        rewarding action instead of an act of restraint. I pair it with streaks, badges,
        and levels so good decisions feel like progress, because they are.
      </p>

      <h2>What I believe</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Saving should feel good.</strong> Motivation beats guilt every time.</li>
        <li><strong>Your data is yours.</strong> Bank connections are read-only, encrypted, and never sold. See my <a href="/security">approach to security</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Clarity over complexity.</strong> A simple daily number you actually understand beats a spreadsheet you dread.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How Buoy works</h2>
      <p>
        Link your accounts in under a minute through <a href="/security">Plaid</a>,
        and Buoy categorizes transactions automatically, surfaces subscriptions, and turns
        each category into a daily count-up allowance. An AI advisor is on hand for the
        "can I afford this?" moments. It’s personal finance that runs itself, and roots
        for you.
      </p>

      <p>
        Questions or feedback? Email
        <a href="mailto:contact@buoy-ai.com">contact@buoy-ai.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--sky-top), var(--surface));
    padding: clamp(48px, 8vw, 88px) 0 clamp(20px, 3vw, 36px);
  }
  .page-hero .container {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
  }
</style>
